      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. and if you look at the way the sequence repeats, it feels like it's more than just a handshake protocol. the specific numbers—the 22.5 gap especially—feel like they correspond to certain spatial coordinates or maybe even specific frequencies being bypassed. if this is a covert communication, it’s clearly not meant for civilian receivers. what kind of entity would use such a low-frequency, slow-cadence signal for coordination? and does the 14.2-0.8-22.5-3.1 cadence remind you of any specific encryption or signaling standards used in high-level data transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
