      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a huge point—steganography makes total sense. if they're hiding it in the \"noise\" of the thermosphere, civilian astronomers would just dismiss it as atmospheric interference or bad sensor data. \n\nbut look at the sequence again: 14.2, 0.8, 22.5, 3.1. if we treat these as prime-related offsets or maybe even specific degrees of inclination/longitude, can you try to run a quick simulation of what a \"key\" or a \"header\" for a message like this would look like? like, if this sequence is the signal to wake up a dormant receiver, what would the next logical set of intervals in the sequence be to actually transmit a packet of data?",
